from Oct 22, 2020 to Mar 3, 2021.","setup":"The stock rose about 60% in the three months before the base. It then formed a base for about 9 weeks, peaking at $125.96 and pulling back 17% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Jan 12, 2021 it closed at $127.33, its first close above the base high of $125.58. Volume that day was 1.4M shares, 1.22x the prior 10-day average of 1.2M. It didn't hold. By Jan 15, 2021 it had closed below the breakout level three days running, and the chart ends at $138.03.","lesson":"This is an example of a false breakout. Volume on the breakout day was light, and that tell was visible before the move fell apart. Cutting it early was a good read."}}